  body: "# BSP contribution condition and industrial-cause exception\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe BSP source
    describes an actual Class 1 or Class 2 contribution route and a separate deemed-satisfaction route where an
    employed earner dies as a result of an industrial accident or prescribed disease.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\
    \nDMG 59013 crosses pages 5–6. No real contribution record, industrial cause or entitlement is determined. The
    source expressly excludes the RP easement at DMG 75031; no pension-year rule is copied into BSP.\n\n## Inspected
    passages\n\n- [DMG 59012, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63e64acce90e0706cd61fb95/dmgch59.pdf#page=5).\n\
    - [DMG 59013, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63e64acce90e0706cd61fb95/dmgch59.pdf#page=5).\n\
    \n## Additional context\n\n- [Context: chapter 59, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63e64acce90e0706cd61fb95/dmgch59.pdf#page=6).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol10-ch59`:
    PDF `71e82cafa85c42d01158e79ffef2753cee93cbf6f70ca25e1f51a3e5e13e5192`; extracted pages `495f463962f1954952a4c175629d05ea9edda5403a3e95cb44d4ce64414beb61`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.706049Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63e64acce90e0706cd61fb95/dmgch59.pdf#page=5
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/bsp-death-date-regime
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The contribution condition is one element of the BSP regime, alongside age and residence
      conditions.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch59/0005
      quote: "59011 [See Memo DMG 02/23] A person whose spouse or civil partner dies1 on or after 6.4.17 will be\n\
        entitled to BSP if\n\n\n1. they are under pensionable age2 when their spouse or civil partner dies3and\n\
        \n\n2. they are ordinarily resident\n\n\n      2.1 in GB or\n\n\n      2.2 in any of the Channel Islands
        where UK law has not been amended as far as is necessary to\n\n      give effect to the provisions of an
        agreement 4\n\n\nwhen their spouse or civil partner dies5and\n\n\n3. the contribution condition is satisfied6
        (see DMG 59012).\n\n\nNote 1: See DMG Chapter 74 for guidance on pensionable age.\n\n\nNote 2: See DMG Chapter
        07 for guidance on ordinarily residence and the Channel Islands.\n\n\n     1 Pensions Act 14, s 30(1)(a);
        2 Pensions Act 1995, Sch 4, Part 1, para 1; 3 Pensions Act 14, s 30(1)(b);\n                           \
        \ 4 BSP Regs, reg 8; SS A Act 92, s 179; 5 Pensions Act 14, s 30(1)(c); 6 s 30(1)(d)\n\n\n\nContribution
        condition"
      locator: DMG 59011
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch59/0005
      quote: "59012 For the purpose of DMG 59011 3., the contribution condition is satisfied if, for at least one
        tax\nyear during the deceased’s working life\n\n\n1. they actually paid Class 1 or Class 2 NI contributions
        1and\n\n\n2. their earnings factor was at least 25 times the LEL for the year 2.\n\n\nNote: The easement
        at DMG 75031 does not apply to BSP.\n\n\n                                                              \
        \           1 Pensions Act 14, s 31(1)(a); 2 s 31(1)(b)"
      locator: DMG 59012
